  speakerName: Lito
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'You''re heading toward Plaza Salcedo and don''t want to make any
    turns.

    In Ilokano, ''agdiretso'' means ''go straight.''

    You can use
    it when giving directions or telling someone to continue forward.

    Listen
    carefully: agdiretso.

    Now, try saying ''agdiretso'' yourself.'
